Yes, except if broda is "x1 is a can of oranges", I don't think {lo se pi mu
mei broda} is a fuzzy set at all. Half a can of oranges is another can of
oranges with its contents cut in half, so it forms {lo se pa mei broda}. (On
the other hand this may ultimately be malgli/malrarbau, which would beg the
question of how to reasonably briefly express "half a can of oranges" in
non-malgli/malrarbau terms.)

You're right, though, that {se te pi mu mei} does make formal sense, it just
has no similarity to its natlang counterpart whatsoever. Consequently
(assuming {mei} still maintains all its places) {pi mu mei} also has no
similarity to its natlang counterpart whatsoever.

Good catch though.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

